{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>מפנק</b> — in place of מעדנים." "<b>ואחריתו</b> — that he is pampered, he will desire to be like a son, and he is of נין, and there is a verb from this noun, and it is ינון (Psalms 72:17), meaning he called him נין, like the matter of \"You are my son\" (Psalms 2:7)."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "The comment appears to explain that מנון/נין denotes son or descendant; the phrase 'ויקרא נין' is rendered hyper-literally; 'והוא מן נין' reads 'he is of נין' as Ibn Ezra's etymological claim linking the pampered servant's end-state to the noun נין."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:27.924369313Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}